From 0012-nouveau-pmu-send-reply-timeout Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Krzysztof Kowalski <krzysztof7kowalski@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 26 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 0012/0013] pmu/gt215: timeout waiting for PMU reply

gt215_pmu_send() waits for the PMU reply with an unbounded
wait_event().  If the PMU is dead (e.g. the firmware never started
because the D3hot->D0 transition failed on the MacBookPro11,3), every
caller blocks forever: the kworker running the pstate work sleeps in D
state indefinitely and the write syscall on the pstate file hangs.

Bound the wait with a 2 s timeout; on expiry clear the stale reply slot
and release the send mutex so the error propagates (-EIO) and later
callers are not wedged behind a held mutex.  Callers already handle
errors (e.g. nvkm_memx_init checks the return value).

Signed-off-by: Krzysztof Kowalski <krzysztof7kowalski@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/nouveau/nvkm/subdev/pmu/gt215.c |   13 ++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/nouveau/nvkm/subdev/pmu/gt215.c	2026-08-27 16:39:35.511907655 +0200
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/nouveau/nvkm/subdev/pmu/gt215.c	2026-08-27 16:39:38.519793396 +0200
@@ -74,7 +74,18 @@
 
 	/* wait for reply, if requested */
 	if (reply) {
-		wait_event(pmu->recv.wait, (pmu->recv.process == 0));
+		if (!wait_event_timeout(pmu->recv.wait,
+					pmu->recv.process == 0,
+					msecs_to_jiffies(2000))) {
+			/* PMU went silent (e.g. failed D3hot->D0 on the
+			 * MacBookPro11,3): clear the stale reply slot and
+			 * release the send mutex, otherwise every later
+			 * caller wedges in D state forever.
+			 */
+			pmu->recv.process = 0;
+			mutex_unlock(&pmu->send.mutex);
+			return -EIO;
+		}
 		reply[0] = pmu->recv.data[0];
 		reply[1] = pmu->recv.data[1];
 	}
